    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1088">

                <pb facs="1210" n="1200" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1224: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-10T22:00:00-04:00">January 10,
                            1944—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>249. Reference your 39, January 3, 9 p.m. For the American members of the London
                    Political Warfare Coordinating Committee:</p>
                <p>We feel that it would be undesirable to take this matter up at the present time
                    with the view to obtaining a decision and that it would be preferable to adhere
                    to the position set forth in the Department’s 8267 of December 31, 7 p.m.<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d1088-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
